IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`

-- Tests for act-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Every expected value is worked out from the text (the section is named beside the assertion) and written before the run.
-- Dates are written Date day month year.

§ `Tests: working out periods of time`

§§ `Table 151 (s 151 (2)): which days a described period includes`

-- item 1: "If a licence begins on the first day of a financial year, the licence is in force on that day."
#ASSERT `s 151 (2), table 151: the period includes the stated day` `beginning at, on or with a stated day`
-- item 2: "does not include the stated day".
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151 (2), table 151: the period includes the stated day` `beginning from or after a stated day`)
-- item 3: "If a person's right to apply for review of a decision ends on the last day of a financial year, the person may apply for review of the decision on that day."
#ASSERT `s 151 (2), table 151: the period includes the stated day` `ending at, by, on or with, or continuing to or until, a stated day`
-- item 4: "ending before a stated day" does not include the stated day.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151 (2), table 151: the period includes the stated day` `ending before a stated day`)
-- item 5: "occurring between 2 events" does not include the days when the events happen.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151 (2), table 151: the period includes the stated day` `occurring between 2 events`)

§§ `s 151 (3): the thing may be done on the stated day`

-- Despite item 2, if the thing may be done within a period after a stated day, it may be done on the stated day.
#ASSERT `s 151 (3): the thing may be done on the stated day` `beginning from or after a stated day` TRUE
-- Where s 151 (3) does not apply, item 2 governs: the period does not include the stated day.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151 (3): the thing may be done on the stated day` `beginning from or after a stated day` FALSE)
-- A period beginning on the stated day includes it, whether or not the thing is to be done within a period after it.
#ASSERT `s 151 (3): the thing may be done on the stated day` `beginning at, on or with a stated day` FALSE
-- A period ending before the stated day does not include it, and s 151 (3) is about periods after a stated day only.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151 (3): the thing may be done on the stated day` `ending before a stated day` TRUE)

§§ `The first and last day of a period of days (s 151 (1), (2))`

-- s 151 (2) Example—item 2: a disallowable instrument described as beginning from 30 June starts to operate on 1 July.
#ASSERT `s 151 (2), table 151: the first day of a period that begins at, on, with or from a stated day` `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2026)
-- A period beginning on 30 June includes 30 June.
-- s 151 (2) Example—item 1: a licence begins on the first day of a financial year (1 July 2026); the licence is in force on that day.
#ASSERT `s 151 (2), table 151: the first day of a period that begins at, on, with or from a stated day` `beginning at, on or with a stated day` (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2026)
-- s 151 (2) Example—item 3: a right to apply for review ends on the last day of a financial year (30 June 2027); the person may apply on that day, because a period ending on a day includes it.
#ASSERT `s 151 (2), table 151: the period includes the stated day` `ending at, by, on or with, or continuing to or until, a stated day`
#ASSERT `s 151 (2), table 151: the first day of a period that begins at, on, with or from a stated day` `beginning at, on or with a stated day` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 6 2026)
-- A period described as ending is not described as beginning, so the text gives no first day.
#ASSERT `s 151 (2), table 151: the first day of a period that begins at, on, with or from a stated day` `ending before a stated day` (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Worked case: thirty days from 2026-01-01.
-- The period begins from 1 January, so it does not include it (item 2): day 1 is 2 January and day 30 is 31 January.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days that begins on or from a stated day` 30 `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- Counted from a period beginning on 1 January (item 1), day 1 is 1 January and day 30 is 30 January.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days that begins on or from a stated day` 30 `beginning at, on or with a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 1 2026)
-- One day from 28 February 2024 is 29 February (a leap year); one day from 29 February 2024 is 1 March.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days that begins on or from a stated day` 1 `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 28 2 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days that begins on or from a stated day` 1 `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2024)
-- Thirty days from 31 December 2025 crosses the year end: day 30 is 30 January 2026.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days that begins on or from a stated day` 30 `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 1 2026)
-- The section applies to periods of 1 day or longer (s 151 (1)): a period of no days, or a negative number, is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days that begins on or from a stated day` 0 `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days that begins on or from a stated day` (0 MINUS 3) `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period described by the way it ends, asked for a last day counted from a beginning, is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days that begins on or from a stated day` 30 `ending before a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Periods that end on, or before, a stated day.
-- 30 days ending on 31 January 2026 (item 3, the stated day is included) begin on 2 January.
#ASSERT `s 151: the first day of a period of days that ends at, by, on or with, or before, a stated day` 30 `ending at, by, on or with, or continuing to or until, a stated day` (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
-- 30 days ending before 1 February 2026 (item 4, the stated day is not included) end on 31 January and begin on 2 January.
#ASSERT `s 151: the first day of a period of days that ends at, by, on or with, or before, a stated day` 30 `ending before a stated day` (Date 1 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 151: the first day of a period of days that ends at, by, on or with, or before, a stated day` 0 `ending before a stated day` (Date 1 2 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151: the first day of a period of days that ends at, by, on or with, or before, a stated day` 30 `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 2 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 151 (2) Example—item 5: a notice of motion is to be served 2 days before the return date; the return date is a Friday (9 January 2026).
-- Neither the return date nor the day of service is counted, so service must be on or before the Tuesday (6 January 2026).
#ASSERT `s 151 (2), table 151 item 5: the latest day for the earlier event, so that the given number of days lie between the 2 events` 2 (Date 9 1 2026) EQUALS Date 6 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 151 (2), table 151 item 5: the number of days between 2 events` (Date 6 1 2026) (Date 9 1 2026) EQUALS 2
-- Served on Wednesday 7 January, only 1 day (Thursday) lies between.
#ASSERT `s 151 (2), table 151 item 5: the number of days between 2 events` (Date 7 1 2026) (Date 9 1 2026) EQUALS 1

§§ `Dictionary: month`

-- Example 1 of the definition: the period beginning at the start of 8 May 2014 and ending at midnight on 7 June 2014 is a month.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 8 5 2014) EQUALS Date 7 6 2014
-- Example 2: the month beginning at the start of 30 January 2014 ends at midnight on 28 February 2014 (2014 is not a leap year).
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 30 1 2014) EQUALS Date 28 2 2014
-- Example 2, continued: if the period began at the start of 30 January 2016 (a leap year), the month would end at midnight on 29 February 2016.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 30 1 2016) EQUALS Date 29 2 2016
-- Limb (a) with a start on the 31st whose next month has a 31st: 31 December 2025 ends immediately before 31 January 2026.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 30 1 2026
-- Limb (b) with a start on the 31st whose next month has only 30 days: 31 March 2024 has no corresponding day in April, so it ends at the end of April.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 31 3 2024) EQUALS Date 30 4 2024
-- Limb (b) with a start on the 31st and February: 31 January 2024 ends at the end of February (29 February, a leap year).
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 31 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- Limb (b) with a start on 29 February: there is no 29 February in the next February, but the next calendar month of 29 February 2024 is March, which has a 29th, so limb (a) applies.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 28 3 2024
-- A month beginning on the 1st ends on the last day of that month.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 31 1 2026
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 1 2 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
-- A month beginning on 15 December ends on 14 January of the next year.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 15 12 2025) EQUALS Date 14 1 2026
-- A month beginning on 1 December ends on 31 December.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of the month that begins at the start of a day` (Date 1 12 2025) EQUALS Date 31 12 2025

§§ `Periods of months (dictionary: month; s 151 (2))`

-- Worked case: one month from 2024-01-31.
-- The period begins from 31 January, so it begins at the start of 1 February (item 2) and ends immediately before the start of 1 March: 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 1 months `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- Worked case: two months from 2025-12-31.
-- The period begins at the start of 1 January 2026; the first month ends on 31 January, the second begins on 1 February and ends on 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 2 months `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- Counted from a period beginning on 31 December 2025 (item 1), the first month ends on 30 January, and the second begins on 31 January and ends at the end of February: 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 2 months `beginning at, on or with a stated day` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- Six months from 15 March 2026 begin on 16 March and end on 15 September 2026.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 6 months `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 9 2026)
-- Three months beginning on 31 August 2025 (s 79, "6 months beginning on its notification day" is of this kind): months end 30 September, 31 October, 30 November.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of a run of successive months, the first beginning at the start of a day` (Date 31 8 2025) 3 EQUALS Date 30 11 2025
-- Six months beginning on 31 August 2025: the months end 30 Sep, 31 Oct, 30 Nov, 31 Dec, 31 Jan, 28 Feb 2026.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of a run of successive months, the first beginning at the start of a day` (Date 31 8 2025) 6 EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- Zero months, or fewer, are not a period of months.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 0 months `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Act defines no unit called a week.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 2 weeks `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The two readings of "N months" agree when the starting day is the 1st to the 28th ...
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of a run of successive months, the first beginning at the start of a day` (Date 16 3 2026) 6 EQUALS Date 15 9 2026
#ASSERT `dictionary, month, other reading: the last day of N months counted to the corresponding day of the Nth following calendar month` (Date 16 3 2026) 6 EQUALS Date 15 9 2026
-- ... and differ after a clamp: starting at the start of 31 January 2024, the first month ends at the end of February (29 February), the second begins on 1 March and ends on 31 March;
-- counted to the corresponding day of the second following month, the period ends immediately before 31 March, that is on 30 March.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of a run of successive months, the first beginning at the start of a day` (Date 31 1 2024) 2 EQUALS Date 31 3 2024
#ASSERT `dictionary, month, other reading: the last day of N months counted to the corresponding day of the Nth following calendar month` (Date 31 1 2024) 2 EQUALS Date 30 3 2024

-- Counting months backwards (the text does not count backwards; this is the month rule read from the other end).
-- s 151 (2) Example—item 4: renewal "not later than 6 months before the day the accreditation period ends", the period ending on 2 November (2026):
-- the 6-month period ending on 1 November 2026 begins on 2 May 2026.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the first day of the month that ends at the end of a stated day` (Date 1 11 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 10 2026)
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the first day of a run of successive months that ends at the end of a stated day` (Date 1 11 2026) 6 EQUALS JUST (Date 2 5 2026)
-- Going forward from the day found, the same six months end where they were required to end.
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the last day of a run of successive months, the first beginning at the start of a day` (Date 2 5 2026) 6 EQUALS Date 1 11 2026
-- No month, as the dictionary defines it, ends at the end of 30 March (it would have to begin on 31 February).
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the first day of the month that ends at the end of a stated day` (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `dictionary, month: the first day of a run of successive months that ends at the end of a stated day` (Date 1 11 2026) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Periods of years (dictionary: year, calendar year)`

-- Calendar year: a period of 12 months beginning on 1 January, so one calendar year beginning on 1 January 2026 ends on 31 December 2026.
#ASSERT `dictionary, calendar year and year: the last day of a run of calendar years beginning at the start of a day` (Date 1 1 2026) 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2026)
#ASSERT `dictionary, calendar year and year: the last day of a run of calendar years beginning at the start of a day` (Date 1 1 2026) 5 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2030)
-- A period of years from 31 December 2025 begins at the start of 1 January 2026 (item 2), so it is a run of calendar years.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 1 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2026)
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 5 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2029)
-- Worked case: three years from 2025-07-16. The period begins at the start of 17 July 2025, which is not the start of a calendar year; the text does not say how many days that is.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 3 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Worked case: five years from 2025-01-15 and from 2025-09-01.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 5 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 5 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 9 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Worked case: one year from 2024-02-29.
#ASSERT `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 1 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Zero years, or fewer, are not a period of years.
#ASSERT `dictionary, calendar year and year: the last day of a run of calendar years beginning at the start of a day` (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- The other reading (12 months to the year, from any starting day) gives the following for the same worked cases.
#ASSERT `s 151, other reading of years: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 3 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 16 7 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 7 2028)
#ASSERT `s 151, other reading of years: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 5 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
#ASSERT `s 151, other reading of years: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 5 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 9 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2030)
#ASSERT `s 151, other reading of years: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 1 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- On every other unit the other reading agrees with the first.
#ASSERT `s 151, other reading of years: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 30 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 151, other reading of years: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` 2 months `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)

§§ `Working days and business days (dictionary; s 151A)`

-- Test calendar (these dates are inputs written for the test, not statements of the Holidays Act 1958):
-- a public holiday on Thursday 1 January 2026, a bank holiday on Monday 5 January 2026,
-- an office closure on Monday 5 January and Tuesday 6 January 2026.
`test calendar` MEANS `Calendar facts` WITH
    `public holidays` IS LIST (Date 1 1 2026)
    `bank holidays` IS LIST (Date 5 1 2026)
    `days when the office is not open` IS LIST (Date 5 1 2026), (Date 6 1 2026)

-- dictionary, working day: not a Saturday or Sunday and not a public holiday in the ACT.
#ASSERT `dictionary, working day: the day is a working day` (Date 2 1 2026) `test calendar`
#ASSERT NOT (`dictionary, working day: the day is a working day` (Date 1 1 2026) `test calendar`)
#ASSERT NOT (`dictionary, working day: the day is a working day` (Date 3 1 2026) `test calendar`)
#ASSERT NOT (`dictionary, working day: the day is a working day` (Date 4 1 2026) `test calendar`)
-- A bank holiday is not a public holiday, so it does not stop a day being a working day.
#ASSERT `dictionary, working day: the day is a working day` (Date 5 1 2026) `test calendar`
-- dictionary, business day: not a Saturday or Sunday and not a public holiday or bank holiday in the ACT.
#ASSERT NOT (`dictionary, business day: the day is a business day` (Date 5 1 2026) `test calendar`)
#ASSERT NOT (`dictionary, business day: the day is a business day` (Date 1 1 2026) `test calendar`)
#ASSERT `dictionary, business day: the day is a business day` (Date 6 1 2026) `test calendar`

-- s 151A (4) (b): for anything else, not a Saturday or Sunday, not a public holiday at the place; for an authorised deposit-taking institution, not a bank holiday either.
#ASSERT `s 151A (4): the day is a working day for doing the thing` (Date 5 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151A (4): the day is a working day for doing the thing` (Date 5 1 2026) `anything else, by or in relation to an authorised deposit-taking institution` `test calendar`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151A (4): the day is a working day for doing the thing` (Date 1 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151A (4): the day is a working day for doing the thing` (Date 3 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar`)
-- s 151A (4) Example—par (a): filing a document at a court registry is something at an office of a public entity.
-- s 151A (4) (a): for something at an office of a public entity, a day when the office is open.
-- The text asks only whether the office is open, so a Saturday on which the office is open counts.
#ASSERT `s 151A (4): the day is a working day for doing the thing` (Date 3 1 2026) `something at an office of a public entity` `test calendar`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151A (4): the day is a working day for doing the thing` (Date 5 1 2026) `something at an office of a public entity` `test calendar`)

-- s 151A (2): the thing is done on the next day that is a working day.
-- Last day Saturday 3 January 2026: the next working day is Monday 5 January.
#ASSERT `s 151A (2): the day on which the thing must or may be done, where the particular day or the last day of the period is that day` (Date 3 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 5 1 2026)
-- Last day Sunday 4 January: also Monday 5 January.
#ASSERT `s 151A (2): the day on which the thing must or may be done, where the particular day or the last day of the period is that day` (Date 4 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 5 1 2026)
-- Last day Thursday 1 January (public holiday): Friday 2 January.
#ASSERT `s 151A (2): the day on which the thing must or may be done, where the particular day or the last day of the period is that day` (Date 1 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
-- A day that is already a working day is unchanged.
#ASSERT `s 151A (2): the day on which the thing must or may be done, where the particular day or the last day of the period is that day` (Date 2 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
-- For an authorised deposit-taking institution, Monday 5 January is a bank holiday: the next working day is Tuesday 6 January.
#ASSERT `s 151A (2): the day on which the thing must or may be done, where the particular day or the last day of the period is that day` (Date 3 1 2026) `anything else, by or in relation to an authorised deposit-taking institution` `test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 6 1 2026)
-- At an office closed on 5 and 6 January, the first day when it is open after a closed day.
#ASSERT `s 151A (2): the day on which the thing must or may be done, where the particular day or the last day of the period is that day` (Date 5 1 2026) `something at an office of a public entity` `test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 7 1 2026)
-- A search that is allowed no days cannot find a working day on a non-working day: the text does not say what then happens.
#ASSERT `s 151A (2): the first working day on or after a day, searching a limited number of days` (Date 3 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 151A (2): the first working day on or after a day, searching a limited number of days` (Date 3 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar` 2 EQUALS JUST (Date 5 1 2026)

-- s 151 and s 151A together: thirty days from 2 December 2025.
-- The period begins on 3 December (item 2); day 30 is Thursday 1 January 2026, a public holiday, so the thing may be done on Friday 2 January 2026.
#ASSERT `s 151 and s 151A: the last day on which the thing may be done within a period that begins on or from a stated day` 30 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 2 12 2025) `anything else` `test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026 end on Saturday 31 January 2026, so the thing may be done on Monday 2 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 151 and s 151A: the last day on which the thing may be done within a period that begins on or from a stated day` 30 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- The rule moving the last day applies to periods of months and years too, because it speaks of "the last day of the period".
-- One month from 31 January 2026 ends on 28 February 2026 (a Saturday), so the thing may be done on Monday 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 151 and s 151A: the last day on which the thing may be done within a period that begins on or from a stated day` 1 months `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
-- A period of weeks is not covered, so nothing follows from s 151A.
#ASSERT `s 151 and s 151A: the last day on which the thing may be done within a period that begins on or from a stated day` 2 weeks `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) `anything else` `test calendar` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests: commencement, repeal, age and service`

§§ `Chapter 8: commencement`

-- Points used below (written for the tests).
`the beginning of 11 January 2026` MEANS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 11 1 2026)

-- s 73 (1) (a): an Act commences on the day after its notification day, at the beginning of that day (s 74 (1)).
#ASSERT `s 73 (1) and s 74 (1): when an Act commences` (Date 1 7 2025) NOTHING EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 2 7 2025)
-- s 73 (1) (b): if the Act or another Act provides a different date, it commences on that date.
#ASSERT `s 73 (1) and s 74 (1): when an Act commences` (Date 1 7 2025) (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 9 2025))) EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 9 2025)
-- s 74 (1): a different time of commencement provided by the Act is used: 9:30 on 2 July 2025.
#ASSERT `s 73 (1) and s 74 (1): when an Act commences` (Date 1 7 2025) (JUST (`Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 2 7 2025, `time of day` IS `stated time` 9 30)) EQUALS `Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 2 7 2025, `time of day` IS `stated time` 9 30

-- s 73 (2): a legislative instrument notified on 10 January 2026 commences, by paragraph (a), at the beginning of 11 January.
#ASSERT `s 73 (2) and (3): when a legislative instrument commences` (Date 10 1 2026) NOTHING `an Act` EQUALS `the beginning of 11 January 2026`
-- (b): a later date provided by the instrument itself.
#ASSERT `s 73 (2) and (3): when a legislative instrument commences` (Date 10 1 2026) (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 20 1 2026))) `the instrument, without authority given by an Act` EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 20 1 2026)
-- (b): a later time on the day after the notification day.
#ASSERT `s 73 (2) and (3): when a legislative instrument commences` (Date 10 1 2026) (JUST (`Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 11 1 2026, `time of day` IS `stated time` 14 0)) `the instrument, without authority given by an Act` EQUALS `Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 11 1 2026, `time of day` IS `stated time` 14 0
-- (c): an Act provides an earlier date.
#ASSERT `s 73 (2) and (3): when a legislative instrument commences` (Date 10 1 2026) (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 1 2026))) `an Act` EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 1 2026)
-- (d): the instrument, under authority given by an Act, provides an earlier date.
#ASSERT `s 73 (2) and (3): when a legislative instrument commences` (Date 10 1 2026) (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 1 2026))) `the instrument, under authority given by an Act` EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 1 2026)
-- (3): an earlier date provided by the instrument without authority is not used; it commences on the day after notification.
#ASSERT `s 73 (2) and (3): when a legislative instrument commences` (Date 10 1 2026) (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 1 2026))) `the instrument, without authority given by an Act` EQUALS `the beginning of 11 January 2026`
-- The date provided equals the date under paragraph (a): it is neither later nor earlier.
#ASSERT `s 73 (2) and (3): when a legislative instrument commences` (Date 10 1 2026) (JUST `the beginning of 11 January 2026`) `the instrument, without authority given by an Act` EQUALS `the beginning of 11 January 2026`

-- s 73 (4): a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument commences on the day after the day it is made ...
#ASSERT `s 73 (4) (a): the day a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument is made or approved` (Date 3 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 3 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 73 (4): when a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument commences` (Date 3 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING `an Act` EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 4 3 2026)
-- ... or, if it must be approved, on the day after the day it is approved.
#ASSERT `s 73 (4) (a): the day a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument is made or approved` (Date 3 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 10 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 73 (4): when a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument commences` (Date 3 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) NOTHING `an Act` EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 11 3 2026)
-- (c): an Act provides an earlier date for it.
#ASSERT `s 73 (4): when a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument commences` (Date 3 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 3 2026))) `an Act` EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 3 2026)

-- s 75: the provisions providing for a law's name and commencement commence on its notification day (10 January 2026) ...
#ASSERT `s 75 (1), (2): when the provisions providing for a law's name and commencement commence` (Date 10 1 2026) (LIST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 15 1 2026)), (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 20 1 2026))) EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 10 1 2026)
-- ... unless a provision commences before that day: they are taken to have commenced on the earliest such commencement.
#ASSERT `s 75 (1), (2): when the provisions providing for a law's name and commencement commence` (Date 10 1 2026) (LIST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 7 1 2026)), (`Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 5 1 2026, `time of day` IS `stated time` 9 0)) EQUALS `Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 5 1 2026, `time of day` IS `stated time` 9 0
-- A provision that commences on the notification day itself does not commence before it.
#ASSERT `s 75 (1), (2): when the provisions providing for a law's name and commencement commence` (Date 10 1 2026) (LIST (`Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 10 1 2026, `time of day` IS `stated time` 9 0)) EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 10 1 2026)
-- s 75 (3): for a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument, the notification day is the day after it is made or approved.
#ASSERT `s 75 (3): the notification day of a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument` (Date 3 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 4 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 75 (3): the notification day of a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument` (Date 3 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 11 3 2026

-- s 75AA (2): the earliest of the commencements of the amendments.
#ASSERT `s 75AA (2): when a provision identifying the amended law commences` (LIST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 8 6 2026)), (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 6 2026))) EQUALS JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT `s 75AA (2): when a provision identifying the amended law commences` (EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 75A (1): the example in s 75B, an Act notified on 1 July 2003 and taken to have commenced on 17 October 2001, commences retrospectively.
#ASSERT `s 75A (1): an Act or legislative instrument commences retrospectively` (Date 1 7 2003) (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 17 10 2001))
-- Commencing at the beginning of the day after the notification day is not retrospective, nor is a later time.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 75A (1): an Act or legislative instrument commences retrospectively` (Date 1 7 2003) (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 2 7 2003)))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 75A (1): an Act or legislative instrument commences retrospectively` (Date 1 7 2003) (`Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 2 7 2003, `time of day` IS `stated time` 9 0))
-- Midnight at the end of 1 July is the time when that day ends, which is when 2 July begins: not earlier than the beginning of 2 July.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 75A (1): an Act or legislative instrument commences retrospectively` (Date 1 7 2003) (`Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 1 7 2003, `time of day` IS `midnight at the end of the day`))
-- 11.59 pm on 1 July is earlier than the beginning of 2 July.
#ASSERT `s 75A (1): an Act or legislative instrument commences retrospectively` (Date 1 7 2003) (`Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 1 7 2003, `time of day` IS `stated time` 23 59)
-- s 75A (2): a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument, made on 3 March 2026, commencing on 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 75A (2): a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument commences retrospectively` (Date 3 3 2026) NOTHING (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 3 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 75A (2): a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument commences retrospectively` (Date 3 3 2026) NOTHING (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 4 3 2026)))
-- Approval is required and given on 10 March: commencing on 6 March is retrospective.
#ASSERT `s 75A (2): a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument commences retrospectively` (Date 3 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 6 3 2026))

-- s 77 (3): the day fixed by a commencement notice (5 January 2026) is before the notice's notification day (10 January): the law commences on the day after.
#ASSERT `s 77 (3), (4): when a law commences under a commencement notice` (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 1 2026)) (Date 10 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the beginning of 11 January 2026`
-- s 77 (3): a time on the notification day itself is "on or before" it.
#ASSERT `s 77 (3), (4): when a law commences under a commencement notice` (`Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 10 1 2026, `time of day` IS `stated time` 9 0) (Date 10 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the beginning of 11 January 2026`
-- s 77 (4): where the notice clearly indicates an earlier commencement under authority given by an Act, subsection (3) does not apply; the day fixed is used.
#ASSERT `s 77 (3), (4): when a law commences under a commencement notice` (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 1 2026)) (Date 10 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 1 2026)
-- A day fixed after the notification day is simply the commencement.
#ASSERT `s 77 (3), (4): when a law commences under a commencement notice` (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 15 1 2026)) (Date 10 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 15 1 2026)

-- s 79 (1): a postponed law notified on 31 August 2025 and not commenced within 6 months beginning on that day:
-- the 6 months end on 28 February 2026, so it commences on 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 79 (1): when a postponed law automatically commences` (Date 31 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 3 2026))
-- Notified on 15 January 2026: the 6 months end on 14 July 2026; it commences on 15 July 2026.
#ASSERT `s 79 (1): when a postponed law automatically commences` (Date 15 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 15 7 2026))
-- Notified on 31 December 2025: the 6 months end on 30 June 2026; it commences on 1 July 2026.
#ASSERT `s 79 (1): when a postponed law automatically commences` (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026))
-- A postponed law that commenced within the 6 months is not caught by s 79 (1).
#ASSERT `s 79 (1): when a postponed law automatically commences` (Date 15 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 81 (6): a legislative instrument notified on 10 January 2026 commences on 11 January.
#ASSERT `s 81 (6): when an appointment or instrument that declares subsection (6) applies commences` TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS `the beginning of 11 January 2026`
-- Any other instrument made on 3 March 2026 commences on 4 March; if it was approved on 10 March, on 11 March.
#ASSERT `s 81 (6): when an appointment or instrument that declares subsection (6) applies commences` FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 4 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 81 (6): when an appointment or instrument that declares subsection (6) applies commences` FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 11 3 2026)
-- s 81 (7): the latest of the commencement of the authorising law (1 July 2026) and the day the appointment would have commenced.
#ASSERT `s 81 (7): when an appointment or instrument made under s 81 commences` (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)) NOTHING (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 15 6 2026)) EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)
#ASSERT `s 81 (7): when an appointment or instrument made under s 81 commences` (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)) NOTHING (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 15 9 2026)) EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 15 9 2026)
-- Where s 81 (1) (b) applies and the amending law commences after the authorising law (1 August 2026), that later commencement is used.
#ASSERT `s 81 (7): when an appointment or instrument made under s 81 commences` (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)) (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 8 2026))) (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 15 6 2026)) EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 8 2026)
-- ... and an amending law commencing before the authorising law is not used.
#ASSERT `s 81 (7): when an appointment or instrument made under s 81 commences` (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)) (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 6 2026))) (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 15 6 2026)) EQUALS `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)

§§ `Chapter 9: repeal`

-- s 85 (3): a law repealed on 30 June 2026 and not remade continues in force until the end of the day; the repeal takes effect at midnight on the day.
#ASSERT `s 85: when the repeal of a law takes effect` (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (`Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 30 6 2026, `time of day` IS `midnight at the end of the day`)
-- s 85 (2): remade on that day: the repeal takes effect when the remade law commences.
#ASSERT `s 85: when the repeal of a law takes effect` (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 30 6 2026))) EQUALS JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 30 6 2026))
-- Remade on that day but the remade law's commencement is not given: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `s 85: when the repeal of a law takes effect` (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 89 (1): the day after all provisions have commenced (5 March) or after the last uncommenced provisions are omitted or cannot commence.
#ASSERT `s 89 (1): the day an amending law is automatically repealed` (JUST (Date 5 3 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 6 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 89 (1): the day an amending law is automatically repealed` NOTHING (JUST (Date 9 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
-- Where both happen, the law is repealed on the day after the first of them.
#ASSERT `s 89 (1): the day an amending law is automatically repealed` (JUST (Date 5 3 2026)) (JUST (Date 9 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 6 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 89 (1): the day an amending law is automatically repealed` (JUST (Date 9 3 2026)) (JUST (Date 5 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 6 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 89 (1): the day an amending law is automatically repealed` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 89 (2): an appropriation Act for the financial year beginning on 1 July 2025 is repealed on the last day of that financial year, 30 June 2026.
#ASSERT `s 89 (2): the day an appropriation Act is automatically repealed` 2025 EQUALS Date 30 6 2026
-- s 89 (3), (4): immediately after the latest commencement.
#ASSERT `s 89 (3), (4): the point in time immediately after which the provision is automatically repealed` (LIST (`Point in time` WITH `day` IS Date 1 7 2026, `time of day` IS `stated time` 9 0), (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 3 7 2026))) EQUALS JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 3 7 2026))
#ASSERT `s 89 (3), (4): the point in time immediately after which the provision is automatically repealed` (EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 89 (5): the day after the last of the days fixed (20 January).
#ASSERT `s 89 (5): the day a commencement notice is automatically repealed` (LIST (Date 10 1 2026), (Date 20 1 2026), (Date 15 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 21 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 89 (5): the day a commencement notice is automatically repealed` (EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 89 (6): the day the last-ending appointment ends.
#ASSERT `s 89 (6): the day an instrument making or evidencing appointments is automatically repealed` (LIST (Date 10 1 2026), (Date 20 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 89 (6): the day an instrument making or evidencing appointments is automatically repealed` (LIST (Date 20 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 1 2026)
-- s 89 (8): a law that would be repealed on 5 January 2026, before its notification day (10 January), is repealed on 11 January.
#ASSERT `s 89 (8): the day a law is automatically repealed, if the day would be earlier than its notification day` (Date 5 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS Date 11 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 89 (8): the day a law is automatically repealed, if the day would be earlier than its notification day` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS Date 10 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 89 (8): the day a law is automatically repealed, if the day would be earlier than its notification day` (Date 12 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS Date 12 1 2026

§§ `Chapter 15: age (s 149)`

-- A person born on 15 June 2000 is 18 years old at the beginning of 15 June 2018.
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 14 6 2018) EQUALS JUST 17
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 15 6 2018) EQUALS JUST 18
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 16 6 2018) EQUALS JUST 18
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 31 12 2017) EQUALS JUST 17
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2018) EQUALS JUST 18
-- A day before the birth is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 14 6 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 15 6 2000) EQUALS JUST 0
-- A person born on 29 February 2000: the birthday for the age 20 is 29 February 2020 (a leap year).
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 28 2 2020) EQUALS JUST 19
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 29 2 2020) EQUALS JUST 20
-- In 2018 there is no 29 February; the text does not say whether the birthday for the age 18 is 28 February or 1 March, so 28 February is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 27 2 2018) EQUALS JUST 17
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 28 2 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 1 3 2018) EQUALS JUST 18
-- The day a person attains an age.
#ASSERT `s 149: the day a person attains an age in years` (Date 15 6 2000) 18 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 6 2018)
#ASSERT `s 149: the day a person attains an age in years` (Date 29 2 2000) 20 EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2020)
#ASSERT `s 149: the day a person attains an age in years` (Date 29 2 2000) 18 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149: the day a person attains an age in years` (Date 15 6 2000) (0 MINUS 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149: the birthday falls in the year` (Date 29 2 2000) 2018 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 149: the birthday falls in the year` (Date 29 2 2000) 2020 EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Chapter 15 and 13: the dates after which some rules are determinative or apply`

#ASSERT `s 146 (4): the application date` `an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument` EQUALS Date 1 1 2000
#ASSERT `s 146 (4): the application date` `any other statutory instrument` EQUALS Date 1 1 2006
-- "after the application date" does not include the application date itself (table 151, item 2).
#ASSERT `s 146 (4): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` `an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument` (Date 2 1 2000) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 146 (4): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` `an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument` (Date 1 1 2000) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 146 (4): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` `any other statutory instrument` (Date 1 1 2006) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 146 (4): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` `any other statutory instrument` (Date 2 1 2006) NOTHING
-- A provision inserted after the application date into an older Act is an applicable provision.
#ASSERT `s 146 (4): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` `an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument` (Date 5 5 1990) (JUST (Date 15 3 2010))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 146 (4): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` `an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument` (Date 5 5 1990) (JUST (Date 1 1 2000)))
-- s 151 (5), s 151A (4), s 151C (6): after 1 January 2006.
#ASSERT `s 151 (5), s 151A (4), s 151C (6): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` (Date 2 1 2006) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151 (5), s 151A (4), s 151C (6): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` (Date 1 1 2006) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151 (5), s 151A (4), s 151C (6): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` (Date 31 12 2005) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 151 (5), s 151A (4), s 151C (6): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` (Date 31 12 2005) (JUST (Date 2 1 2006))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 151 (5), s 151A (4), s 151C (6): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` (Date 31 12 2005) (JUST (Date 1 1 2006)))
-- s 126 (2): the heading to a section or subsection is part of the Act if it was enacted after 1 January 2000, or the heading was amended or inserted after that day.
#ASSERT `s 126 (2): the heading to a section or subsection is part of the Act or instrument` (Date 2 1 2000) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 126 (2): the heading to a section or subsection is part of the Act or instrument` (Date 1 1 2000) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 126 (2): the heading to a section or subsection is part of the Act or instrument` (Date 5 5 1990) (JUST (Date 5 5 2010))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 126 (2): the heading to a section or subsection is part of the Act or instrument` (Date 5 5 1990) (JUST (Date 1 1 2000)))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 126 (2): the heading to a section or subsection is part of the Act or instrument` (Date 5 5 1990) NOTHING)

§§ `Part 19.5: when a document is taken to be served (s 250)`

-- s 250 (1): a document served by post is taken to be served when it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post (an input: the text gives no number of days).
#ASSERT `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served` `by sending it by prepaid post` (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 6 3 2026)) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 6 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served` `by sending it by prepaid post` (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 250 (3): a fax or email is presumed served when sent, if the sender has no reason to suspect it was not received ...
#ASSERT `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served` `by fax` (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served` `by email` (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
-- ... unless evidence sufficient to raise doubt about the presumption is given.
#ASSERT `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served` `by email` (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- If the sender has reason to suspect it was not received, the text does not say when it is served.
#ASSERT `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served` `by fax` (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served` `by fax` (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 250 (5): a document left at an address is taken to be served when it was left.
#ASSERT `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
-- Giving a document to the person: the text gives no rule about when it is served.
#ASSERT `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served` `by giving it to the person, or to an executive officer` (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 250 (4): the sender has reason to suspect only if the equipment indicated a failure on the day sent or the next working day.
#ASSERT `s 250 (4): the sender has reason to suspect the document was not received` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 250 (4): the sender has reason to suspect the document was not received` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The next working day after Wednesday 31 December 2025 skips the public holiday on Thursday 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `dictionary, working day: the first working day after a day, searching a limited number of days` (Date 31 12 2025) `test calendar` 10 EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
#ASSERT `dictionary, working day: the first working day after a day, searching a limited number of days` (Date 2 1 2026) `test calendar` 10 EQUALS JUST (Date 5 1 2026)
#ASSERT `dictionary, working day: the first working day after a day, searching a limited number of days` (Date 2 1 2026) `test calendar` 1 EQUALS NOTHING
